[3mincluding their current status from the payment provider. The implementation is [0m
[3mfunctionally correct but contains a performance anti-pattern that will degrade [0m
[3munder load.[0m

[1;31mF1  HIGH  [0m [1mN+[0m[1;36m1[0m[1m network calls in loop[0m  [2morderflow/api/refunds.py:[0m[1;2;36m27[0m
     The loop iterates over all refunds and calls `[1;35m_provider_status[0m[1m([0mrefund[1m)[0m` for
each one, which makes a separate network request to the payment provider per 
refund. If an order has many refunds, this will cause significant latency and 
potential rate-limiting issues. Consider batching the status requests if the 
provider supports it, or caching the status if it doesn't change frequently.

